'' See the source's header. fbc compiles all four shapes -- measured on 1.20.0, the
'' equivalent program prints 'inner', 'outer', 5 then 7 -- and tiko refused the first
'' two with TKO0630 while reading them as a member access of a pointer.
''
'' The member-access cases are in the same file deliberately: the rule turns on whether
'' the base is a PROCEDURE, so a variable base has to come through untouched or the fix
'' has traded one wrong reading for another.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/namespace-dot-argument.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0630
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0600
